{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1857","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1857","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1857\",\"parent_revision\":\"d78b7e235c607e7ad157fb340a4012bbe88fa380\",\"root_revision\":\"d3ad19d1d610032002f0f780bf511bf4d532296b7870eef7716c64712fcb5ce3\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Verdict: APPROVED-WITH-GAPS**\\\\n\\\\n| Input | Status | Source |\\\\n|---|---|---|\\\\n| Functional intent | AVAILABLE | Item description + Target state section |\\\\n| Scope boundaries | AVAILABLE | Opt-in `ac-gate: true`; auto-skip when `acceptance_criteria` is empty |\\\\n| External interfaces | AVAILABLE | `sam_task` MCP, `marko` parser, `task.notes` field, `sam_task(action='state')` |\\\\n| Constraints | DERIVABLE | Non-breaking opt-in; must not block plans without the flag |\\\\n| Existing system context | AVAILABLE | Verified: `task-worker.md`, `task_status_hook.py` (lines 167-199), `models.py` (lines 197-201), `implement-feature/SKILL.md` Step 4 |\\\\n| Verification expectations | AVAILABLE | `sam_task(action='read')` -> `status: blocked` + `notes` field; `tests_sam/test_ac_gate.py` |\\\\n\\\\n**Gap \u2014 Plan model flag support**: The item specifies `ac-gate: true` as a plan-level flag. Whether the `Plan` model in `sam_schema/core/models.py` supports this field is DERIVABLE by reading the Plan class. If unsupported, the opt-in mechanism needs an alternative design (task-level field, skill argument, env var). This gap affects opt-in mechanism design only, not the core AC parsing or gate logic.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **add acceptance-criteria validation gate before task-worker marks complete** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Research entry: ./research/agent-frameworks/orchestra.md \u2014 limitation 5: No built-in validation of agent output quality\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-04-20\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-21)\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n7/10 \u2014 Direct integrity gap in the SAM task lifecycle. Workers can declare completion without meeting stated acceptance criteria, undermining the value of writing AC at all. Downstream consumers (`complete-implementation`, `contract-verification`, `feature-verifier`) trust task status as a quality signal. False positives propagate through the full quality gate pipeline.\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n- Blocks: Quality signal integrity for all SAM-planned features using `implement-feature`\\\\n- Bottleneck: `feature-verifier` and `complete-implementation` receive misleading task state when workers self-report completion despite failing AC\\\\n- Affected components: `implement-feature/SKILL.md` Step 4 (insertion point), `task-worker.md` Step 5 (unchecked completion path), `task_status_hook.py` SubagentStop handler, `sam_schema/core/models.py` Plan model (may need ac-gate flag field)\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n- Adds a falsification test to the completion path: AC must be verifiably met, not just defined\\\\n- Prevents downstream quality gate pollution with false-green tasks\\\\n- Consistent with the strict hook profile design intent (which checks AC defined but not met, stopping short of evaluating items)\\\\n- Reduces fix-in-quality-gates rework by catching failures at the point of task completion\\\\n- Closes the gap shared with Orchestra limitation 5 (no built-in output quality validation \u2014 research/agent-frameworks/orchestra.md lines 417-421)\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nWhen a task-worker completes work on a plan where `ac-gate: true` is set and the task has non-empty `acceptance_criteria`:\\\\n\\\\n- A `dh:ac-gate` agent runs after the task-worker returns but before concerns accumulation (Step 4 of `implement-feature`)\\\\n- The agent reads the task's `acceptance_criteria` string, extracts checklist items (`- [ ] ...` format) via `marko`\\\\n- For each checklist item, the agent produces a pass/fail verdict using task output evidence (modified files list, test run output)\\\\n- If all items pass: task state remains `complete` and the normal pipeline continues\\\\n- If any item fails: task state transitions to `blocked`; failing AC item text is written to `task.notes`\\\\n- When `acceptance_criteria` is empty: gate is skipped automatically, task state is unchanged\\\\n- When the plan does not have `ac-gate: true`: gate is not invoked, behavior is identical to today\\n\\n### Desired Structure\\n\\n- New `dh:ac-gate` agent at `plugins/development-harness/agents/ac-gate.md`\\\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/implement-feature/SKILL.md` Step 4 modified: conditionally invoke `dh:ac-gate` between task-worker return and concerns accumulation\\\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/models.py` Plan model extended with `ac-gate` boolean field (or equivalent opt-in mechanism, pending Plan model review \u2014 see Blockers)\\\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests_sam/test_ac_gate.py` integration test: dummy worker returns COMPLETE with unmet AC, asserts task ends in `blocked`\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. A plan with `ac-gate: true` and a task whose worker wrote a passing unit test plus one failing lint check results in `sam_task(action='read')` showing `status: blocked` after the worker exits\\\\n2. The `notes` field of the blocked task contains the specific failing AC item text verbatim\\\\n3. `tests_sam/test_ac_gate.py` exists and passes: dummy worker returns COMPLETE with an unmet AC, asserts final task status is `blocked`\\\\n4. A plan without `ac-gate: true` runs through `implement-feature` unchanged \u2014 `dh:ac-gate` is never invoked, task state is set by the existing SubagentStop hook\\\\n5. A task with empty `acceptance_criteria` on an `ac-gate: true` plan is not blocked \u2014 the gate skips gracefully\\\\n6. Existing `implement-feature` integration tests pass without modification (backward compatibility guaranteed)\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\\\n|------|------|\\\\n| Agent | @dh:contract-verification \u2014 parallel pattern for post-task verification in implement-feature Step 4a; same insertion point |\\\\n| Agent | @dh:feature-verifier \u2014 complementary goal-backward verification (plan-level, not task-level) |\\\\n| Skill | /dh:implement-feature \u2014 insertion point is Step 4 (after task-worker return, before concerns accumulation) |\\\\n| Skill | /dh:validation-protocol \u2014 validation patterns and checklists |\\\\n| Prior work | `plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/task_status_hook.py` lines 167-199: `run_strict_pre_completion_checks()` \u2014 checks AC defined but never evaluates items; direct predecessor pattern |\\\\n| Prior work | `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/models.py` lines 197-201: `Task.acceptance_criteria` \u2014 free-text str field, no checklist parsing |\\\\n| Prior work | `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/quality_gates.py`: `build_proportional_quality_gate_plan()` generates Phase 3 \\\\\\\"Acceptance Criteria Check\\\\\\\" as manual agent-executed task \u2014 precedent for AC verification as a distinct agent step |\\\\n| Prior work | `plugins/development-harness/agents/task-worker.md` Step 5: unchecked self-reported completion via `sam_task(action='state', status='complete')` |\\\\n| Prior work | `research/agent-frameworks/orchestra.md` lines 417-421: Limitation 5 \u2014 source pattern this item closes |\\\\n| Library | `marko` \u2014 markdown AST parser for checklist item extraction; already a declared dependency pattern in `.claude/rules/` |\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: None \u2014 no blocking backlog items identified. `marko` is already a declared pattern (`.claude/rules/` markdown AST rule). `sam_task` MCP and `task.notes` field are already in production.\\\\n- Blocks: None identified. Items using `implement-feature` (#1089 semantic compaction, #1770 incremental task append) are not gated on this gate's insertion.\\n\\n### Blockers\\n\\n- **Plan model opt-in mechanism unverified**: whether the `Plan` class in `sam_schema/core/models.py` supports an `ac-gate` boolean field must be checked before finalizing the opt-in design. If absent, alternatives are: (1) task-level metadata flag, (2) implement-feature skill argument, (3) `CLAUDE_SKILLS_AC_GATE=true` env var. Read the `Plan` class definition to resolve before implementation starts.\\\\n- **Evidence evaluation strategy undefined**: the target state says the ac-gate agent evaluates AC against \\\"task output evidence (modified files, test output artifact).\\\" How test output artifacts are passed to the agent \u2014 test run stdout piped from SubagentStop context? an artifact registry entry written by task-worker? \u2014 is not specified. This design decision requires resolution in the planning phase before task decomposition.\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nMedium \u2014 Core logic (markdown parsing via `marko`, status transition to `blocked`, notes field write) maps directly to existing patterns in `task_status_hook.py` and `contract-verification`. The new `dh:ac-gate` agent is bounded scope. Two design decisions must be resolved first (Plan model field availability, evidence evaluation strategy) but neither requires external dependencies or new infrastructure.\\n\\n## Target State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nA new `dh:ac-gate` agent runs in `implement-feature` Step 4 (after task-worker returns, before concerns accumulation). It reads `task.acceptance_criteria`, extracts checklist items (`- [ ] ...` via `marko`), and for each item produces a verdict using task output evidence (modified files, test output artifact). If any item fails, the task is transitioned to `blocked` instead of `complete` and failing items are written to the task's `notes` field. Opt-in via plan-level `ac-gate: true`; opt-out automatic when `acceptance_criteria` is empty.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Measurable Signal\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- Against a plan with `ac-gate: true` and a task whose worker wrote a passing unit test plus one failing lint, `sam_task(action='read')` after the worker exits shows `status: blocked` and `notes` contains the specific failing AC item text.\\n- Integration test `tests_sam/test_ac_gate.py` runs a dummy worker that returns COMPLETE with an unmet AC and asserts the task ends in `blocked`.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Current State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`task-worker.md` Step 5 marks a task complete via `sam_task(action='state', status='complete')` on the worker's own judgement. The SubagentStop hook (`task_status_hook.py`) observes completion and writes the `Completed` timestamp. The `strict` hook profile (`plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/SKILL.md` lines 208\u2013211) checks that AC were *defined* and that the task was claimed, but never checks that AC were *met*. The `acceptance_criteria` field (models.py line 197) is a free-text string; nothing parses its checklist items against artifact evidence.\\n\\nSymptom: a worker can write a failing test and still call `state=complete`. Downstream consumers (complete-implementation, contract-verification) see a green task and move on. This is the exact gap the Orchestra research entry documents as limitation 5 \u2014 we share it.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"9992ac5cade5c0c69d7c68fce0b28d5b338238b433676d0e58fd33b1629f54d0\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPnJIog\"}"}